	'ab_label' => 'About the distillery',
	'ab_title' => 'About Taruki Distillery',
	'ab_intro' => 'Founded in 2016 by head distiller Mira Okafor, Taruki Distillery produces small-batch coastal gin on Quarry Lane in Larchmere. Our craft is anchored in patient copper pot distillation and close partnerships with local growers.',
	'ab_1_t' => 'The First Cut That Went Down the Drain (2016)',
	'ab_1_b' => 'When Mira Okafor established Taruki Distillery in 2016, our copper still Ottilie arrived without an operational manual. During our very first distillation run, the balance between heads, hearts, and tails proved elusive. Determined never to bottle compromised spirit, Mira diverted the entire distillation run down the drain. That costly decision set our enduring standard: we only bottle cuts that meet our exacting sensory criteria, regardless of production volume or schedule pressure.',
	'ab_2_t' => 'Peel from the Hillside Grove (2019)',
	'ab_2_b' => 'In 2019, an unseasonal spring frost threatened the coastal citrus crop on the hills overlooking Larchmere harbour. Working alongside citrus grower Samir Haddad, we harvested surviving lemons and bitter oranges by hand, developing our signature gentle peel-drying method. That harvest became the foundation of our Larchmere Citrus Peel Gin, turning an agricultural challenge into our most celebrated botanical profile through mutual trust and patience.',
	'ab_3_t' => 'Why Ottilie Runs Slowly (2023)',
	'ab_3_b' => 'By 2023, rising demand tempted us to shorten distillation cycles on our three-hundred-litre pot still. Still operator Tomasz Wren conducted side-by-side trials, proving that accelerating the burn stripped the gentle oils of maritime sea fennel and scorched delicate citrus aromatics. We reaffirmed our foundational rule: Ottilie must always run at a gentle, unhurried pace. Nine days per batch remains our non-negotiable rhythm, ensuring every bottle reflects true craft.',
	'ab_4_t' => 'Our Philosophy and Six-Year Timeline',
	'ab_4_b' => 'Head distiller Mira Okafor founded the distillery with a singular premise: craft gin should taste of the maritime soil, harbour salt, and coastal sun where it is made. Across key milestone years from 2016 through 2018, 2019, 2021, 2022, and 2023, we expanded our botanical partnerships while strictly limiting batch size to four hundred and twenty bottles. We remain an independent harbour distillery dedicated to slow copper distillation and honest hospitality.',
