	'pp_intro' => 'Meet the seven dedicated individuals behind Taruki Distillery, from our copper still room and foraging trails to the tasting room bar. We are distillers, growers, and hosts united by our passion for honest craft spirits.',
	'pp_1_t' => 'Mira Okafor, Founder and Head Distiller',
	'pp_1_b' => 'Mira Okafor founded Taruki Distillery in 2016 after years of studying traditional pot distillation. As head distiller, Mira oversees recipe development, botanical selection, and makes every critical sensory cut at Ottilie\'s collection spout. Her commitment to patience, unhurried distillation, and uncompromising quality defines our house style, ensuring that every batch of four hundred and twenty bottles reflects the true maritime character of Larchmere.',
	'pp_2_t' => 'Tomasz Wren and Inès Dubreuil',
	'pp_2_b' => 'Still operator Tomasz Wren manages the daily operation of our three-hundred-litre copper still Ottilie, carefully monitoring steam flow and condenser temperatures throughout our nine-day production cycles. Working alongside him is Inès Dubreuil, our botanical forager, who gathers wild sea fennel from the rocky harbour shore and selects dried juniper, angelica, and spices. Inès ensures all botanicals meet strict aromatic standards before they enter our maceration vats.',
	'pp_3_t' => 'Kenji Halvorsen and Ana Lucía Ferro',
	'pp_3_b' => 'Kenji Halvorsen leads our tasting room team, welcoming guests Wednesday through Sunday and mixing balanced drinks that highlight our spirits\' botanical profiles. Working closely with visitors is tour guide Ana Lucía Ferro, who conducts our distillery tours. Ana Lucía translates technical distillation concepts into engaging stories, walking guests through our still room from botanical tables to the tasting room bar with warmth and clarity.',
	'pp_4_t' => 'Ruth Abernathy and Samir Haddad',
	'pp_4_b' => 'Ruth Abernathy oversees our bottling bench, hand-filling every bottle, securing natural wood stoppers, and writing individual batch numbers on our paper labels. On the hills above Larchmere harbour, citrus grower Samir Haddad manages the Hillside Grove. As our agricultural partner since 2019, Samir cultivates the lemon and bitter orange trees that yield the vibrant, oil-rich citrus rinds central to our flagship gin.',
	'pp_more_l' => 'Also at the distillery',
	'pp_5_n' => 'Ana Lucía Ferro',
