	'vi_label' => 'Visit',
	'vi_title' => 'Visit the Distillery',
	'vi_intro' => 'Located at 14 Quarry Lane in Larchmere, our working harbour distillery and tasting room are open Wednesday through Sunday. We invite you to experience our slow copper distillation in person.',
	'vi_1_t' => 'Hours and Weekly Rhythm',
	'vi_1_b' => 'The tasting room welcomes visitors Wednesday through Sunday from eleven-hundred until eighteen-hundred hours. On Monday and Tuesday, our tasting room and shop doors are closed to the public while our copper still Ottilie continues running uninterrupted. Guided distillery tours depart Wednesday through Sunday at eleven-thirty, fourteen-hundred, and sixteen-hundred hours. We recommend reserving tours in advance, as group sizes are strictly limited to twelve visitors.',
	'vi_2_t' => 'Location and Getting Here',
	'vi_2_b' => 'Taruki Distillery is located at 14 Quarry Lane in the harbour town of Larchmere, set just beneath the terraced citrus groves of the hillside. Visitors arriving by public transit will find local bus connections running regularly from the central harbour station to the Quarry Lane stop, followed by a short level walk to our gates. Bicycle racks are available beside our courtyard entrance, and visitor vehicle parking is located directly on site.',
	'vi_3_t' => 'Accessibility and Facilities',
	'vi_3_b' => 'Our tasting room, bottle shop, courtyard, and ground-floor still room are step-free and fully accessible to wheelchair users. Accessible restroom facilities are situated immediately adjacent to the tasting room. Because our still room is an active industrial production environment with warm pipes and operating machinery, children under eighteen are welcome only in our bottle shop and outdoor courtyard, while guided production tours remain strictly reserved for visitors aged eighteen and over.',
	'vi_band_h' => 'Wednesday to Sunday, 11:00–18:00',
	'vi_band_p' => 'Closed Monday and Tuesday while Ottilie keeps running.',
	'vi_f1_l' => 'Address',
	'vi_f1_v' => '14 Quarry Lane, Larchmere',
	'vi_f2_l' => 'Tasting room',
