	'vi_end_h' => 'Come for the tour, stay for the glass',
	'vi_end_cta' => 'Book a visit',
	'nl_intro' => 'Subscribe to our monthly newsletter for quiet dispatches from our still room, seasonal botanical reports, and advance notice of new bottle allocations. We write once per month directly from Larchmere.',
	'nw_1_t' => 'What We Share in Each Issue',
	'nw_1_b' => 'The Batch Letter is a concise, monthly publication written directly by our distillers and growers. Each dispatch includes updates on current distillation runs in Ottilie, botanical foraging observations from the Larchmere shoreline, and citrus harvest reports from Samir Haddad at the Hillside Grove. We also share early release announcements for limited gin batches before bottles become available to the public in our tasting room.',
	'nw_2_t' => 'Subscription Details and Privacy',
	'nw_2_b' => 'We respect your inbox and send only one letter each month. We never share subscriber email addresses with external parties or transmit unsolicited marketing messages. You can unsubscribe at any moment through the single-click link included at the foot of every email. Enter your email address in the field provided to receive our next dispatch directly from our harbour still room on Quarry Lane.',
	'ct_label' => 'Contact',
	'ct_title' => 'Contact Us',
	'ct_intro' => 'Reach out to our distillery team with questions about tours, bottle orders, or private tastings. We are based on Quarry Lane in Larchmere and respond to all inquiries within one working day.',
	'ct_1_t' => 'Distillery Address and Operating Hours',
	'ct_1_b' => 'Taruki Distillery is situated at 14 Quarry Lane, Larchmere. Our tasting room and bottle shop are open Wednesday through Sunday from eleven-hundred to eighteen-hundred hours. On Monday and Tuesday, our doors are closed to visitors while our still runs. If you wish to reach us by telephone, our team can be contacted at plus zero zero one two three four five six seven eight during normal tasting room operating hours.',
	'ct_2_t' => 'Inquiries and Direct Messages',
	'ct_2_b' => 'For general questions, tour inquiries, or bespoke private event requests, please submit your message through the form on this page. If you prefer to contact us using your own email software, write directly to hello@taruki-distillery.example. Kenji Halvorsen and our tasting room staff review all incoming communications daily, ensuring you receive a clear, thoughtful response within one working day of your message.',
	'fq_label' => 'Questions',
	'fq_title' => 'Frequently Asked Questions',
	'fq_intro' => 'Find clear answers to common questions regarding distillery visits, age requirements, dietary considerations, and reservation policies. If you need further assistance, our team is always ready to help.',
	'fq_1_q' => 'What is the minimum age requirement for distillery tours and tastings?',
	'fq_1_a' => 'All participants joining our guided distillery tours, cut tastings at the still, or botanical blending workshops must be at least eighteen years of age. We enforce this policy strictly to comply with licensing laws and ensure safety around active distillation equipment. Visitors may be asked to present valid government photo identification upon arrival before participating in spirits tastings.',
	'fq_2_q' => 'Are children and guests under eighteen permitted to visit?',
	'fq_2_a' => 'Guests under eighteen years of age are warmly permitted to visit our bottle shop and outdoor courtyard garden when accompanied by an adult guardian. However, due to the industrial nature of our working still room with high steam temperatures and moving machinery, minors are strictly prohibited from entering production areas or participating in scheduled tours, tasting flights, or blending sessions under any circumstances.',
	'fq_3_q' => 'How should designated drivers handle spirits tastings during a tour?',
	'fq_3_a' => 'We actively support designated drivers visiting our harbour distillery. Drivers participating in any of our guided tours are welcome to enjoy non-alcoholic refreshments during the session. Tour guide Ana Lucía Ferro will provide specially prepared miniature tasting sample bottles so that drivers can safely take home their designated spirit measures to savour at their leisure after completing their journeys.',
	'fq_4_q' => 'What is your cancellation and rescheduling policy for booked visits?',
	'fq_4_a' => 'We require at least forty-eight hours advance notice if you need to cancel or reschedule your tour booking. Cancellations received with forty-eight hours or more notice will receive a full refund or a voucher to rebook for a future date. Cancellations made with less than forty-eight hours notice are non-refundable, as each session is strictly capped at twelve guests to preserve an intimate experience.',
	'fq_5_q' => 'Are dogs and other pets allowed inside the distillery?',
	'fq_5_a' => 'Well-behaved dogs on leads are welcome in our outdoor courtyard seating area and within the front bottle shop. However, because our still room is an active food and beverage production facility governed by strict hygiene and environmental health regulations, animals other than registered guide dogs and assistance animals are not permitted inside the production still room or primary indoor tasting room spaces.',
	'fq_6_q' => 'How do you accommodate guests with botanical allergies or dietary concerns?',
	'fq_6_a' => 'All Taruki gins are distilled from neutral grain spirit infused with nine botanical ingredients: juniper, fresh Larchmere lemon peel, bitter orange, coriander seed, angelica root, Florentine orris root, aromatic bay leaf, pink pepper, and wild sea fennel. If you have known allergies to specific herbs, tree fruits, or citrus varieties, please notify our team when submitting your booking request so we can advise you.',
	'fq_7_q' => 'How many guests can join a public or private distillery tour?',
	'fq_7_a' => 'To maintain an engaging, calm, and conversational environment inside our still room, public tour groups are strictly capped at twelve guests per scheduled session. For private group bookings, we accommodate parties of up to ten guests, providing exclusive access to Ottilie and personalised guidance from our distillers. Larger groups cannot be accommodated in a single tour session due to spatial constraints around our equipment.',
	'fq_8_q' => 'What days and hours are the tasting room and bottle shop open?',
	'fq_8_a' => 'Our tasting room and bottle shop operate Wednesday through Sunday from eleven-hundred until eighteen-hundred hours. We are closed to the public on Monday and Tuesday, which allows still operator Tomasz Wren and head distiller Mira Okafor to run distillation batches without interruption. Guided tours take place Wednesday through Sunday at eleven-thirty, fourteen-hundred, and sixteen-hundred hours, and must be booked in advance.',
	'fq_9_q' => 'Can I purchase bottles directly at the distillery during my visit?',
	'fq_9_a' => 'Yes, our complete range of spirits is available for direct purchase in our bottle shop on Quarry Lane during standard opening hours. Visitors can purchase our flagship Larchmere Citrus Peel Gin in seventy-centilitre bottles at forty-four euros and our Navy Cut Gin in fifty-centilitre bottles at forty-nine euros. Bottling lead Ruth Abernathy can also assist with custom handwritten gift cards for your purchases.',
	'fq_10_q' => 'Is the distillery accessible for visitors with limited mobility?',
	'fq_10_a' => 'Yes, our distillery facility is designed to be accessible for all visitors. The courtyard, bottle shop, tasting room bar, and ground-floor still room pathways are entirely step-free and accommodate wheelchairs and walking aids comfortably. An accessible restroom is located on the ground floor next to the tasting room. Please mention any specific accessibility requirements when booking your tour so our team can prepare.',
